From: OpenWrt MR80X v2 port
Subject: mtd: spinand: esmt: do not register the OTP areas

Kernel 6.18 added OTP support for the ESMT F50L1G41LB and F50D1G41LB. On the
Mercusys MR80X v2 (IPQ5018, QPIC SPI NAND) that support bricks all flash access.

Declaring SPINAND_USER_OTP_INFO/SPINAND_FACT_OTP_INFO makes spinand_init()
call spinand_set_mtd_otp_ops(), and MTD registration then creates the
user-otp and factory-otp nvmem devices. The resulting OTP access leaves
CFG_OTP_ENABLE set on the chip while the driver's cfg_cache says it is clear.
Because spinand_upd_cfg() skips the register write whenever the cached value
already matches, every later attempt to leave OTP mode becomes a no-op, and
no warning is printed.

From then on the chip serves its OTP area instead of the array: page 0 returns
the unique ID page, page 1 the ONFI parameter page, everything above reads as
0xff. Reads report no error because the hardware erased-page detector
legitimately flags those pages as blank, and writes fail with -EIO. The effect
looks exactly like a wiped or unreadable flash, which is what made this hard
to spot. Observed on the device:

  spinanddbg: cfg as found at probe = 00 (otp_en=0)   first probe, chip is clean
  spinanddbg: cfg as found at probe = 40 (otp_en=1)   second probe, OTP left on
  spinanddbg: OTP off: cached=00 chip=40 -> chip=00   cache and chip disagree

Forcing the register write restores normal operation immediately and the flash
content is intact, so nothing is damaged, it is purely a mode the chip is left
in. 6.12 is unaffected because it carries no OTP support for these parts.

Drop the OTP declarations for both ESMT entries. The feature is not used on
this hardware and the rest of the chip support is unchanged.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c
@@ -208,9 +208,7 @@
 					      &write_cache_variants,
 					      &update_cache_variants),
 		     0,
-		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f50l1g41lb_ooblayout, NULL),
-		     SPINAND_USER_OTP_INFO(28, 2, &f50l1g41lb_user_otp_ops),
-		     SPINAND_FACT_OTP_INFO(2, 0, &f50l1g41lb_fact_otp_ops)),
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f50l1g41lb_ooblayout, NULL)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("F50D1G41LB",
 		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_ADDR, 0x11, 0x7f,
 				0x7f),
@@ -220,9 +218,7 @@
 					      &write_cache_variants,
 					      &update_cache_variants),
 		     0,
-		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f50l1g41lb_ooblayout, NULL),
-		     SPINAND_USER_OTP_INFO(28, 2, &f50l1g41lb_user_otp_ops),
-		     SPINAND_FACT_OTP_INFO(2, 0, &f50l1g41lb_fact_otp_ops)),
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f50l1g41lb_ooblayout, NULL)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("F50D2G41KA",
 		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_ADDR, 0x51, 0x7f,
 				0x7f, 0x7f),
